"Modern skills are usually designed to rapidly reproduce a difficult but desirable spell."
"Skills are more flexible than spell impressions and reach complex results, but are harder to learn."
"Most modern skills top out between Levels 4 and 10; Level 10 means mastery."
"A maxed skill is complete, and its holder picks a new one."
"Leveling a skill once a year is common; twice is standard at Apex schools; many never level."
"A skill user's perception of the skill shapes what it can do."
"Summoners see Avowed abilities as data on their displays, such as a preservation talent."
"Skill names and descriptions on Earth are vague because a thousand committees shaped them."
"Skills can be read as spell code, and each species gets a redesigned version."
"Some skills top out at level 5, others at 10."
